    <h1 class="project-hero-title">Synapse → Microsoft Fabric OneLake migration</h1>
    <p class="project-hero-lede">Moved a global retail client's warehouse from Azure Synapse to Microsoft Fabric OneLake - rebuilt for the new storage model rather than lifted and shifted, with reconciliation on every migrated table.</p>
    <dl class="def-list project-facts">
      <dt>Role</dt><dd>Data Engineer - ODS replication, migration design and delivery</dd>
      <dt>Period</dt><dd>Jan 2023 - Nov 2024</dd>
      <dt>Stack</dt><dd>Azure Synapse · Microsoft Fabric OneLake · Databricks · Azure Data Factory · SQL</dd>
      <dt>Outcome</dt><dd>Downstream reporting stayed available through the cutover</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>The retail client's warehouse ran on Azure Synapse with metadata pipelines that needed to scale further, and 50+ transactional tables were still coupling downstream reporting directly to the operational system - adding load and slowing everything behind it.</p>
      <h2>Approach</h2>
      <p>I replicated the 50+ transactional tables into an operational data store, taking read load off the source system so downstream reporting no longer queried it directly. From there the warehouse moved onto Microsoft Fabric OneLake - rebuilt for the new storage model rather than lifted and shifted, with row-level reconciliation against source on every migrated table.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="meta-mono" style="margin-top:32px">Azure Synapse → Microsoft Fabric OneLake, with Databricks and Azure Data Factory driving ingestion throughout.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Results</p></div>
    <dl class="def-list" style="margin-top:32px">
      <dt>Uptime</dt><dd>99.9% maintained across pipeline operations, supporting rapid scaling for high-volume data.</dd>
      <dt>Scalability</dt><dd>Replicating 50+ transactional tables reduced system load and enabled faster scaling for downstream consumers.</dd>
      <dt>Integrity</dt><dd>Migration preserved data integrity while optimizing the underlying storage architecture.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

